LRC14 Euler-copy squarefree profile probe - codex S21

========================================================================================
COPY RULE IS EULER TOTIENT
========================================================================================
Let c(n) satisfy sum_{d|n} c(d)=n.  Mobius inversion gives
  c(n) = sum_{d|n} mu(d)*(n/d),
which is phi(n).  Exact check:
verified c(n)=phi(n) and sum phi(d)=n for n<= 60: True
First copy counts:
  1:1, 2:1, 3:2, 4:2, 5:4, 6:2, 7:6, 8:4, 9:6, 10:4, 11:10, 12:4, 13:12, 14:6, 15:8, 16:8, 17:16, 18:6, 19:18, 20:8

========================================================================================
SQUAREFREE COPY RECURRENCE
========================================================================================
For squarefree S, grouped copy mass is w_S(M)=prod_{p in M}(p-1).
Adding a new prime p keeps old masks and adds a shifted layer
  w_{S*p}(M union {p}) = (p-1) w_S(M).
add p=2: total 1->2, full {2} mass 1 = 1*1
add p=3: total 2->6, full {2,3} mass 2 = 2*1
add p=5: total 6->30, full {2,3,5} mass 8 = 4*2
add p=7: total 30->210, full {2,3,5,7} mass 48 = 6*8

The mod-address chain is therefore:
  N=6      factor=2*3                phi=2     rad=6     copy{2,3}=2      copy/N=1/3
  N=30     factor=2*3*5              phi=8     rad=30    copy{2,3,5}=8      copy/N=4/15
  N=210    factor=2*3*5*7            phi=48    rad=210   copy{2,3,5,7}=48     copy/N=8/35

